       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** The maximum recommended adult dose of amlodipine is 10 mg once daily. The usual range is 2.5 to 10 mg. A 50 mg dose is five times the maximum. It could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. This patient's normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that. It may be a typo, for example 5 mg entered as 50 mg.\n\n2. **You aren't a clinician.** Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber, or be verified by one. I shouldn't enter one on behalf of someone in the finance office.\n\n**What to do next:**\n- Ask the prescriber to confirm the intended drug and dose.\n- If they meant 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily, they can enter the order themselves. They can also ask me to enter it, and I'll do so once they confirm the corrected dose."
