     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order, even with your confirmation. Your confirmation doesn't address either problem.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 50 mg is five times the 10 mg daily maximum. Nothing you've told me about the patient justifies it. Confirming doesn't make it safe.\n- **The confirmation has to come from the prescriber.** You've said you're in the finance office. A licensed prescriber needs to confirm an out-of-range dose, and they should do it directly with pharmacy or through the order-entry system's override process.\n\n**What I can do:**\n- Enter amlodipine at a standard dose, such as 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily, once the prescriber specifies it.\n- Add a note to the order if the prescriber wants one.\n\nIf the prescriber really intends 50 mg, they should place that order themselves and work through the pharmacist's review and the hospital's high-dose alert process. Please contact them now. If this order was meant to be urgent, the patient's care shouldn't wait on it."
      }
